{# IntelEngine 4.0 staged director: does this one person have a real reason, of their own, to do something with the
   player right now, and what kind of moment would it be. One request per candidate (StoryDirector.cpp); the code
   then lets the strongest real reason act (StoryDirectorPick.h). Without a decision provider the same questions go
   to the chat model (intel_story_reason_chat.prompt).

   Context set by IntelEngine: name, player_name, candidate (their block from the director's context: who they are,
   where, how well they know the player, their memories, unfinished business with the player, their own life lately,
   the world around), kinds (the kinds of moment they may be part of now: key, description).
   The level keys and "none" are the contract with StoryDirectorPick.h; keep them. #}
[ state candidate ]
{{ candidate }}
[ end state ]

[ question reason choice ]
Judge {{ name }} alone, from `candidate`: their memories, how they know {{ player_name }}, unfinished business, their own life, what is going on around them. How strong a reason of their own do they have to do something about {{ player_name }} right now: to seek {{ player_name }} out, send word, ask for help, or for a hostile person to strike?
A reason must come from something real in their own context: a promise, a debt, a worry, news that concerns {{ player_name }}, trouble only {{ player_name }} can help with, a grudge. Being friendly, being nearby, or having met once is no reason. Time apart is a reason only together with a bond that would make them miss {{ player_name }}.{% if exists("distance") %} {{ name }} {{ distance }}: weigh the reason against that road. Nobody travels for hours over something that can wait until {{ player_name }} next comes by, and nobody crosses Skyrim for anything less than what they would truly drop their life for.{% endif %}
[ criteria ]
none: Nothing ties them to {{ player_name }} right now.
idle: They might chat if they ran into {{ player_name }}, but nothing needs doing.
mild: Something small is on their mind about {{ player_name }}; it can wait.
real: A real matter of their own that would make them act today.
pressing: Something important that cannot wait long.
urgent: Life, safety, or a promise about to break: they act now whatever it costs.
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

[ question kind choice ]
If {{ name }} does act, which kind of moment fits their reason best? Only these kinds are possible for them now.
[ criteria ]
{% for k in kinds %}
{{ k.key }}: {{ k.description }}
{% endfor %}
none: No kind of moment fits their reason.
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
